&lt;p&gt;The Iran-backed Houthis have told the Donald Trump administration that they will not target US vessels in the Red Sea, while warning other countries against joining Saudi Arabia in Yemen&amp;rsquo;s escalating conflict.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mohamed al-Bukhaiti, a member of the Houthis&amp;rsquo; political bureau, told The Associated Press that Washington reached out to the group after its rapid advance along Yemen&amp;rsquo;s western coast towards the Bab el-Mandeb Strait earlier this month. He said the Houthis assured US officials that their operations were not directed at the United States or other countries using the strategic waterway.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;We confirmed that we are not targeting the United States, or any other nation, in the strait, with the sole exception of the Saudi enemy,&amp;rdquo; al-Bukhaiti said in an interview from Sanaa.&lt;/p&gt;
